        "ruleBudget": 4,
        "overrideDefaultPolicy": true,
        "defaultPolicy": "Deny"
      },
      "persona": "Blackhat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Reyes Calloway:</b> Build the policy they asked for. Default deny, minimal exceptions, and nothing left open that you cannot justify in a single sentence.\n\nI will say the quiet part. A tight boundary here is worth more to me than a sloppy one, because sloppy gets torn up and rewritten by somebody more careful in six months. Done once, it stays the shape you gave it.",
      "taskInstructions": "Rules match source, port, and protocol from top to bottom; the first match wins and unmatched traffic falls through to default deny. Press TEST when all six requests are handled correctly.",
      "taskQuestion": "Build the default-deny boundary policy.",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Reyes Calloway:</b> The first-match policy permits the documented internal flows and leaves every tested external request to default deny."
    },
